scene intro
  line "Ignacio Ruelas: \"The border is a wound that never heals. I was born on one side, my family buried on the other. I fight for the land, not the line.\""
scene camp
  line "Ignacio Ruelas: \"Down in El Paso, the Salt War is brewing. The Anglos want the salt flats. The Tejanos have worked them for generations. Something's going to give.\""
scene camp
  line "Ignacio Ruelas: \"My abuela used to say a man without a horse was half a man. Out here, a man without a good rifle is half a dead man.\""
scene mission
  line "Ignacio Ruelas: \"I know this country. Follow me, and I'll keep you out of the worst of it.\""
scene mission
  line "Ignacio Ruelas: \"Listen — that's not the wind. That's horses. We've got company.\""
